Antilles wrote:
> Here's my question:  because I compulsively delete the entire game,
> there's never a bones file full of good stuff from dead adventurers.
> How much of a handicap is that, if any?  Playing on the NAO server
> isn't really an option owing to the dodginess of my connection.

A casual recollection of ascension posts seems to indicate that many
people have a bones-assisted game as their first win, but they can also
make the game considerably harder.  There's nothing preventing that
game with the player who summoned Yeenoghu at an altar on level 4 from
leaving a bones file, and there's nothing to say that it won't continue
to leave bones several games in a row.

It probably means more deaths, but players who survive the perils will
be better prepared, so it also can mean an earlier first ascension.

> Last question:  What does "foo" signify?  Thanks.

"Foo" is a generic placeholder word among computer programmers.  Its
origins were in the old Smokey Stover comic strip
(http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Smokey_Stover), which contained several
nonsense words and phrases whose true and definite meaning were never
revealed.  Foo, in particular, has passed into popular (and especially
programmer) culture, but Nethack also contains a fortune cookie that
says "notary sojac".

